Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:38:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Library viewer: an inferred contents shows the sections it
 does not list

The Contents tab drew an entry's contents entries and nothing else. On
10665-75211 the inferred contents are Part 1's contents pages (70
entries); the 30 chapters and annexes of Parts 2 and 3, cut inside its
last entry by the oversized split, and the front matter were named by no
entry and appeared nowhere in the tree, so the tab read as flat and one
book of three.

With INFERRED contents, each section no entry names is placed among the
entries by its first page, at its own level, and says it is not listed;
the note counts them. 10665-75211 now shows 70 entries and 31 such
sections, two levels deep. An outline is the PDF's own and is shown as
before (its test is unchanged).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPfb62Puokdy7SvkiNR
